# Per-machine Bazel overrides. Copy to .bazelrc.local (which is NOT tracked,
# because the right path differs on every machine) and edit to taste.
#
# WHY: a full run of this repo builds ~1300 test binaries plus 84 ASan twins.
# Measured footprint under ~/.cache/bazel: 8.9 GB. A 42 campus machine usually
# caps $HOME at 5 GB and gives you no sudo, so the default location cannot work
# there — the build fails partway with a disk error that does not name the cause.
#
# Point Bazel's ENTIRE state somewhere with room. This one flag covers the
# output base, the install base and the repository cache; there is no need to
# set them separately.
#
# Use a path that is yours alone: /tmp is shared, and two students pointing at
# the same directory will fight over the same lock.
startup --output_user_root=/tmp/bazel-CHANGEME

# Two more live in your shell profile rather than here, because they are
# ENVIRONMENT variables and not Bazel flags. Both still land under $HOME by
# default, so setting only the flag above leaves a 5 GB quota short:
#
#     export BAZELISK_HOME=/tmp/bazelisk-$USER
#
#         Bazelisk downloads Bazel itself (~63 MB) to ~/.cache/bazelisk.
#
#     export SUBMIT_GATE_OUTPUT_BASE=/tmp/bazel-gate-$USER
#
#         //tools:submit runs its pre-push gate on a SEPARATE output base, so a
#         half-finished edit in your main workspace cannot change what gets
#         pushed. It passes --output_base explicitly, and that OVERRIDES the
#         --output_user_root set above — so this is the one path the flag
#         cannot move for you. Left at its default it is a second full tree
#         under $HOME.
